<http://www.spektrix.com/capilanouniversity/event/23801AJTHHRQPTBGSQKNGJHMKGQMHTHHM>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Florian Hoefner Trio";
  schema:description """
	Born in Germany, trained in New York City and now based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, Juno-winning jazz pianist and composer Florian Hoefner draws from myriad influences that cumulate in his unique brand of modern jazz. Praised by the <span class=\"ItalicText\">New York Times</span> as a “composer-bandleader of insightful resolve” and a “harmonically daring pianist reaching toward new sonic territory,” by <span class=\"ItalicText\">Downbeat</span>, Hoefner has made his mark as an inventive creator and performer.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Hoefner’s trio features Andrew Downing on bass and Nick Fraser on drums. Their 2023 Juno-winning album <span class=\"ItalicText\">Desert Bloom</span>. includes original compositions that showcase Hoefner’s hallmark lyricism. Their previous album, the Juno-nominated First Spring focuses on Hoefner’s arrangements of folk tunes from around the world.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>“In every situation, the music is so substantial and at times even breathtaking.” <span class=\"ItalicText\">Ottawa Citizen</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jF-KNTHzzYA\">Warch Video Here</a>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-04-19T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/capilanouniversity/files/69e08946-a1bb-457a-a2e2-1a3e7f2ee46f.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/capilanouniversity/location/601APNNMRMBJQQPBSCNQGQHGKKCRPSSGN>;
  schema:organizer <https://spektrix.com/capilanouniversity/organization/blueshore-financial-centre-for-the-performing-arts>;
  schema:offers _:c6b4b1028eff4381af491812ccede69e6352;
  schema:keywords "CapU Jazz";
  schema:duration "PT120M";
  schema:endDate "2027-04-19T21:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

